Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:27:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 099/144] GreatDANE: in-tree guard against the retired legacy
 --deep signing paths (steering round 3)

There are no in-tree copies of the legacy $G/sign-only.sh, build-universal.sh or notarize.sh: not in the
ESR153 source tree and not on this branch. The only in-tree signing entry points are
greatdane/tools/sign-only.sh (it refuses any argument, so there are no legacy modes) and
sign_dane_macos.py, which is called by finish-universal.sh.

greatdane/tests/no_legacy_deep_sign_check.py fails if any greatdane/ script (tests excluded):
- signs with codesign --deep (verify --deep is allowed);
- references the blanket browser.entitlements.plist;
- calls $G/sign-only.sh, $G/build-universal.sh or $G/notarize.sh.
It also fails if taskcluster/config.yml has a mac-signing group with `deep: true`, so `mach macos-sign` can
never deep-sign; all 11 groups are deep: false. PASS on this branch. A negative self-check (planted
script) gives 3 hits.

The live Mac scripts are NOT touched. The retirement plan and shims for them are delivered as files
outside the tree (round3 artifacts).
